meta {
  name: Deployment Uses Private Template (200)
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/v1/deployments
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{other_access_token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "name": "Test Deployment with Private Template",
    "template_version_id": "{{private_version_id}}",
    "course_id": "{{course_id}}",
    "deployment_mode": "per_course",
    "heat_parameters": {
      "instance_name": "test-instance"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  # Deployment Uses Private Template Version

  Test that deployments can use any template version (including private) when explicitly specified.

  **Expected:** 200 OK - deployment created successfully

  **Setup:**
  - Use non-owner user credentials
  - Specify private template version ID explicitly
  - Provide valid parameters

  **Verifies:**
  - Deployment creation bypasses template ownership check
  - Users can deploy from any template version if they have the ID
  - Access control exception for deployment use case works

  **Important:**
  This is a special exception - while users cannot browse or list private templates,
  they CAN deploy them if they know the exact template version ID.
  This allows sharing of template versions without making them fully public.
}
